#!/bin/bash
# Compares the lexer generated from test/zig/zig.grammar with
# std.zig.Tokenizer (the Zig that runs this script) token for token: tag by
# name, start and end, invalid tokens included, up to and including eof.
#
# Usage:
#   test/zig/compare-tokens [options] (DIR|FILE|--list LIST)...
#   test/zig/compare-tokens --fuzz N [--seed S]
#
#   DIR             every *.zig file under DIR
#   --list LIST     the paths in LIST, one per line (paths may hold spaces)
#   --oracle BIN    compare with the output of a zigtok binary instead of
#                   std.zig.Tokenizer in process (`BIN --list`, format
#                   `# path bytes` then `tag start end` per token; both
#                   dumps stay in the build directory when a file differs)
#   --fuzz N        compare on N random inputs instead (up to 511 bytes,
#                   std.zig.Tokenizer's fuzz-test byte weights alternating
#                   with a mix of token fragments; --seed S, default 0)
#   --bench N       time tokenizing alone instead, both lexers, best of N
#                   rounds (ReleaseFast, single thread, files in memory)
#   --dump nexus|std  print one lexer's stream in the zigtok format
#   -O MODE         optimize mode of the tool (default ReleaseFast)
#
# The tool is built in .zig-cache/nexus-test/zig-tokens/ from this
# checkout's bin/nexus (run `zig build` first). Compare prints one line per
# input whose streams differ, with the first difference, and a summary with
# the longest token; it exits 1 when any file differs. A token longer than
# 65535 bytes, the most a Nexus token holds, is lexed as `err` over the
# same bytes; a file whose only such differences are these is listed as
# LONG, not counted as differing.

set -uo pipefail
HERE=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
ROOT=$(cd "$HERE/../.." && pwd)
OUT="$ROOT/.zig-cache/nexus-test/zig-tokens"
MODE=ReleaseFast ORACLE="" TOOL_ARGS=() FUZZ=0
LIST="$OUT/list.txt"
mkdir -p "$OUT"
: >"$LIST.new"
while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
    case $1 in
        --list) cat "$2" >>"$LIST.new"; shift ;;
        --oracle) ORACLE=$2; shift ;;
        --bench) TOOL_ARGS+=(--bench "$2"); shift ;;
        --dump) TOOL_ARGS+=(--dump "$2"); shift ;;
        --fuzz) TOOL_ARGS+=(--fuzz "$2"); FUZZ=1; shift ;;
        --seed) TOOL_ARGS+=(--seed "$2"); shift ;;
        -O) MODE=$2; shift ;;
        -h|--help) awk 'NR > 1 { if (!/^#/) exit; sub(/^# ?/, ""); print }' "$0"; exit 0 ;;
        -*) echo "unknown option $1" >&2; exit 2 ;;
        *)
            if [[ -d $1 ]]; then
                find "$(cd "$1" && pwd)" -name '*.zig' -type f | LC_ALL=C sort >>"$LIST.new"
            elif [[ -f $1 ]]; then
                echo "$(cd "$(dirname "$1")" && pwd)/$(basename "$1")" >>"$LIST.new"
            else
                echo "no such file or directory: $1" >&2; exit 2
            fi ;;
    esac
    shift
done
mv "$LIST.new" "$LIST"
[[ -s $LIST || $FUZZ == 1 ]] || { echo "no input files" >&2; exit 2; }

# Build: generate the lexer, compile the tool next to it.
NEXUS="$ROOT/bin/nexus"
[[ -x $NEXUS ]] || { echo "$NEXUS not found: run zig build" >&2; exit 2; }
(cd "$HERE" && "$NEXUS" zig.grammar "$OUT/parser.zig") >"$OUT/gen.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$OUT/gen.log" >&2; exit 2; }
cp "$HERE/zig.zig" "$HERE/tools/tokens.zig" "$OUT/"
(cd "$OUT" && zig build-exe -O "$MODE" tokens.zig -femit-bin=tokens --cache-dir "$ROOT/.zig-cache/nexus-test/zig") \
    >"$OUT/compile.log" 2>&1 || { cat "$OUT/compile.log" >&2; exit 2; }

if [[ -z $ORACLE ]]; then
    [[ $FUZZ == 1 ]] && exec "$OUT/tokens" "${TOOL_ARGS[@]}"
    exec "$OUT/tokens" ${TOOL_ARGS[@]+"${TOOL_ARGS[@]}"} --list "$LIST"
fi

# Against a zigtok binary: both dumps, compared file by file.
"$OUT/tokens" --dump nexus --list "$LIST" >"$OUT/nexus.tok" || exit 2
"$ORACLE" --list "$LIST" >"$OUT/oracle.tok" || exit 2
perl -e '
    sub load {
        my ($f) = @_; my (%h, @order, $cur);
        open my $fh, "<", $f or die "$f: $!\n";
        while (<$fh>) {
            chomp;
            if (/^# (.*) \d+$/) { $cur = $1; push @order, $cur; $h{$cur} = []; next }
            push @{$h{$cur}}, $_;
        }
        return (\%h, \@order);
    }
    my ($n, $order) = load($ARGV[0]);
    my ($o) = load($ARGV[1]);
    my ($differ, $long, $tokens) = (0, 0, 0);
    for my $p (@$order) {
        my ($a, $b) = ($n->{$p}, $o->{$p} // []);
        my $len = @$a > @$b ? @$a : @$b;
        for my $i (0 .. $len - 1) {
            my ($x, $y) = ($a->[$i] // "(ended)", $b->[$i] // "(ended)");
            next if $x eq $y;
            my @x = split / /, $x; my @y = split / /, $y;
            if ($x[0] eq "err" && @y == 3 && $x[1] == $y[1] && $x[2] == $y[2] && $y[2] - $y[1] > 65535) {
                print "LONG $p: token $i: oracle $y (", $y[2] - $y[1], " bytes) is a Nexus err token\n";
                $long++;
                next;
            }
            print "DIFF $p: token $i: nexus $x | oracle $y\n";
            $differ++;
            last;
        }
        $tokens += @$b;
    }
    printf "%d files, %d differ, %d with a token over 65535 bytes, %d tokens (against %s)\n",
        scalar @$order, $differ, $long, $tokens, $ARGV[2];
    exit($differ ? 1 : 0);
' "$OUT/nexus.tok" "$OUT/oracle.tok" "$ORACLE"
rc=$?
[[ $rc -eq 0 ]] && rm -f "$OUT/nexus.tok" "$OUT/oracle.tok"   # kept for inspection when a file differs
exit $rc
